  "_about": "Services a domain's DNS TXT records show it uses. A service asks its customer to publish a verification token, and a mail sender must be named in the domain's SPF record, so these records name vendors the domain depends on even when no other stored relationship does. A verification prefix matches the start of a TXT record (case-insensitive); an SPF domain matches an include: or redirect= mechanism of a v=spf1 record when the mechanism's domain is that domain or ends with it. A token or include can outlive the service, so these are evidence of use, not proof of a current contract. Add vendors here, not in Go code.",
